      "side": 1,
      "message": "This block can be refactored as follows by passing `int64_t* sse` array instead of `PSNR_STATS* psnr` array.\n```\n  sse[pass] \u003d 0;\n  const int num_planes \u003d av1_num_planes(cm);\n  for (int plane \u003d 0; plane \u003c num_planes; plane++) {\n    sse[pass] +\u003d aom_get_sse_plane(cpi-\u003esource, \u0026cm-\u003ecur_frame-\u003ebuf, plane,\n                                   cm-\u003eseq_params-\u003euse_highbitdepth);\n  }\n  sse[pass] +\u003d !sse[pass];\n  if (pass !\u003d 1) return;\n\n  const double psnr_diff \u003d 10 * log10(((double)sse[0]) / sse[1]);\n```\n\nThe uploaded change maintains bit-exactness in scenarios where input bit-depth and codec bit-depth are same.\n\nThe refactored suggestion takes fewer computes and involves lesser float operations making psnr_diff result more accurate but not identical to base version. During a local run, a comparison of psnr_diff from uploaded version and refactored version was made and the result is identical for 12 significant digits.\n\nCan you please suggest which is preferable. Thank you.",
